<title>GERMANY: E. German Dec industrial orders rise 0.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>E. German Dec industrial orders rise 0.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +0.2	 +4.4	-21.8</p>
<p> Year-on-year			-0.9	-22.6	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		131.4	131.2	132.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Dec 96    Nov 96    Dec 96 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     +1.1	+1.9     151.3</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Sept/Oct 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +2.5 @</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Nov/Dec 96 with Nov/Dec 95:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		 -16.9</p>
<p> Domestic orders			-19.9</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +1.2</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +8.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			  -39.0</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -3.8</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
